# Script to Panel

When converting a standalone Studio script into a panel in this plugin framework, follow this pattern:

## 1. Create the tool module

Put all side-effect logic (no UI) in `src/<ToolName>.luau`.

```lua
local ToolName = {}

function ToolName.doSomething(instance: Instance)
    -- side effect logic here
end

return ToolName
```

## 2. Create the panel component

Add `src/Components/<ToolName>Panel.luau` using the shared framework components:

```lua
local Selection = game:GetService("Selection")
local React = require(script.Parent.Parent.Packages.React)

local Panel = require(script.Parent.Panel)
local Header = require(script.Parent.Header)
local SelectionButton = require(script.Parent.SelectionButton)
local Theme = require(script.Parent.Theme)
local ToolName = require(script.Parent.Parent.ToolName)

local e = React.createElement
local useState = React.useState
local useEffect = React.useEffect

local function ToolNamePanel(props)
    local selectedInstance, setSelectedInstance = useState(nil)
    local collapsed, setCollapsed = useState(false)

    useEffect(function()
        local function onSelectionChanged()
            local sel = Selection:Get()
            local target = nil
            for _, obj in sel do
                if obj:IsA("YourTargetClass") then
                    target = obj
                    break
                end
            end
            setSelectedInstance(target)
        end
        onSelectionChanged()
        local conn = Selection.SelectionChanged:Connect(onSelectionChanged)
        return function() conn:Disconnect() end
    end, {})

    -- Gate visibility: return nil if nothing relevant is selected
    if not selectedInstance then
        return nil
    end

    return e(Panel, { layoutOrder = props.layoutOrder }, {
        Header = e(Header, {
            title = "Tool Name",
            collapsed = collapsed,
            onToggle = function() setCollapsed(not collapsed) end,
            layoutOrder = 1,
        }),
        Content = if collapsed then nil else e("Frame", {
            Size = UDim2.new(1, 0, 0, 0),
            AutomaticSize = Enum.AutomaticSize.Y,
            BackgroundTransparency = 1,
            LayoutOrder = 2,
        }, {
            Layout = e("UIListLayout", {
                Padding = UDim.new(0, 2),
                SortOrder = Enum.SortOrder.LayoutOrder,
            }),
            ActionBtn = e(SelectionButton, {
                text = "Do Something",
                layoutOrder = 1,
                backgroundColor = Theme.ACCENT.Action,
                onActivated = function()
                    ToolName.doSomething(selectedInstance)
                end,
            }),
        }),
    })
end

return ToolNamePanel
```

## 3. Register in PanelStack

Open `src/Components/PanelStack.luau` and:
- Add a `require` for your new panel at the top.
- Add it as a child of the ScrollingFrame with a unique `layoutOrder`.

```lua
local ToolNamePanel = require(script.Parent.ToolNamePanel)
-- ...
ToolName = e(ToolNamePanel, { plugin = props.plugin, layoutOrder = N }),
```

## 4. Build

```bash
rojo build --plugin <name from default.project.json>.rbxmx
```

## Reference

See the real-world example in [dhaynes-studio-super-plugin](https://github.com/dhaynes-rbx/dhaynes-studio-super-plugin):
- Tool module: `src/TerrainMover.luau`
- Panel: `src/Components/TerrainMoverPanel.luau`
